From 9b0c3a583bab1675dfdd4c9d60da7b0431583e28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Janniaux <ajanni@videolabs.io>
Date: Wed, 8 Mar 2023 17:50:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 093/105] input: es_out: reset buffering on PCR discontinuity

When PCR discontinuities happens, the whole pipeline is reset and it
safely (though after a glitch) reset back to playback on what's visible
after the PCR discontinuities, and restart buffering.

However, this PCR discontinuity currently happens only when **not** in
buffering. When it happens during buffering, the computed stream buffer
duration goes negative and the buffering either stops far too early or
never converges, counting the time the stream would need to catch up
with a reference that is already in the future.

Instead, if PCR is going back to the past, flush the pipeline and reset
the buffering back to zero to avoid waiting for the stream to catch-up
with the old reference, and avoid buffering more than what we requested,
which would shift the playback more from the live.

Adapted for 3.0, whose EsOutChangePosition takes only the flush flag -
there is no per-ES argument to pass, so the call becomes the two-argument
form. The 3.0 function does what the 4.0 one does here: it flushes the
decoders, resets each program's clock and puts the es_out back into
buffering. Both callers of this function already test b_buffering, and
the repeat path reaches EsOutChangePosition with the flag clear, so
nothing that carries a timeline across a repeat is reached from here.

(cherry picked from commit 07d8bc705da7fbb84344340d91504840b3300674)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/input/es_out.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/input/es_out.c b/src/input/es_out.c
index 61cae4b217..745001b1e5 100644
--- a/src/input/es_out.c
+++ b/src/input/es_out.c
@@ -792,6 +792,17 @@ static void EsOutDecodersStopBuffering( es_out_t *out, bool b_forced )
                                   &i_stream_duration, &i_system_duration ))
         return;
 
+    /* If demux signals PCR going back in time while we were buffering,
+     * we want to reset the pipeline, and reset buffering back to zero
+     * so that we don't compare a reference from the future against
+     * values from the past, which could artifically and arbitrarily
+     * increase the buffering duration. */
+    if (i_stream_duration < 0)
+    {
+        EsOutChangePosition(out, true);
+        return;
+    }
+
     vlc_tick_t i_preroll_duration = 0;
     if( p_sys->i_preroll_end >= 0 )
         i_preroll_duration = __MAX( p_sys->i_preroll_end - i_stream_start, 0 );
